## 3. THE NEXT BLOCKER — main-CSpace cap quota (C3 workstream)

PROVEN failure under the C2 fix (run 2, lines 432-435):

  [pkg_runtime] Warning: falkon: no route to service "RM" (label="falkon -> ")
  [falkon] Error: stop because parent denied RM-session: label="",
                 ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2

ROOT CAUSE (code path traced, not speculated):

  falkon's main CSpace has 32768 slots (C1 fix: CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST=6,
  CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND=9, total 2^15=32768). falkon's init-donated cap
  quota is 30000 (from pkg/falkon metadata). WebEngine creates thousands
  of threads, IPC endpoints, dataspaces, and RM sessions — each consuming
  a main-CSpace cap. falkon burned through ~29998 of 30000 caps and
  pkg_runtime can no longer create the RM session falkon requests
  (only 2 caps remain; an RM session needs more).

  This is the MAIN CSPACE (CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2), INDEPENDENT of the vm_space
  selector pool (NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2=17, 131072 — plenty) that C2 just fixed.
  The vm_space holds page-frame caps; the main CSpace holds IPC/session
  caps. falkon needs both enlarged; C1+C2 fixed vm_space, C3 must fix the
  main CSpace.

  The C1 fix enlarged the main CSpace 8192→32768 (a factor of 4). falkon
  needs strictly more — the plan's C3 step prescribes LAZY 2nd-level
  main-CSpace CNode creation (grow on selector consumption, base-hw
  upgrade_cap_slab philosophy), exactly the pattern C2 just proved for
  vm_space.

  Evidence the vm_space fix is NOT the issue: zero "out of selector" /
  zero "mapping cache full" in run 2. The "denied RM-session cap_quota=2"
  is a pure main-CSpace cap-accounting failure, surfacing only AFTER
  rom_pkg's payload is fully served (the C2 layer is clean).

