## 4. Vendored changes for the docs/11 patch ledger (C4 writes the row)

C4 will add the docs/11-environment.md ledger row. The vendored surface
this workstream introduces (all under genode/repos/base-sel4/, gated to
x86_64 where applicable, other arches upstream byte-for-byte):

  WHAT  : Lazy vm_space CNode growth + enlarged leaf CNodes (131072
          selectors/PD on x86_64, upstream 32768).
  WHERE : vm_space.h (LEAF_CNODE_SIZE_LOG2 7→9 on x86_64; +_core_cnode_sel
          member; +_ensure_leaf lazy construction hook; _leaf_cnode calls
          _ensure_leaf; Construct_cnode::destruct no-op-safe; constructed()
          simplified to vm_pad-only; constructor eager loop removed;
          destructor restructured for lazy; _for_each_l3_cnodes removed);
          platform.cc (core virt_size capped to 256 MiB on x86_64);
          spec/x86_64/platform.cc (16K pool +32 MiB for vm leaves,
          MAX_VM_LEAF_COUNT=2048).
  WHY   : base-sel4 capped each PD's vm_space at 32768 page-frame selectors
          (NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2=15), blocking falkon (~100k frames) and rom_pkg
          (~130k frames) at the "mapping cache full / out of selector"
          stage. Eager enlargement broke boot (heap starvation, silent
          Platform() crash — p4-cspace-fix.log §4). Lazy construction
          avoids all eager-failure modes: the _cnodes[] array stays at
          upstream size, leaves are built on demand from the 16K pool.
  DROP  : revert the 3 files; upstream base-sel4 behaviour is restored
          (32768 selectors, eager construction, 256 KiB core virt). When
          upstream Genode grows lazy vm_space CNodes, this patch is
          obsolete.

Non-vendored (Sponge-owned, no ledger row): run/sponge-falkon-disk.run
rom_pkg caps 2000→20000 (config fix unmasked by the C2 vm_space fix).

